 "text": "Buying a laptop soon? AI is making it pricier. You're up against AI data centers for memory chips and losing. In the US, computers are up almost 10% in a year after 20 years of getting cheaper, give or take a pandemic. Mostly because memory chips cost about five times last year's price. AI data centers need mountains of them and they pay more. It's less of a shortage, more of an auction, and you're bidding against a building. The bids are still climbing, so the cheap laptops drop out first. Experts give it a year or two. That's how a data center ends up on your next laptop's price tag.",
